  reason (compute_stats is 3 % of it now).

=================== WHERE THE 127x WAS (the breakdown that was the plan) ===================

callgrind's callee tree for the old `__arcane_compute_stats_impl_v3` was
ONE self-cost node: 746,546,730 self, 3,986,376 in `__memset` (3,090 calls
= one `h_acc` zero per region row), nothing else — `find_average`, the
window gather and the 50 `mac_row_i32_v3` calls per pixel were all inlined,
so there was no callee to name. Read from the source instead (the shape the
realimg record asked for): per source pixel the arm gathered the `win x win`
window with `win2` strided scalar loads, then ran `win2 + 1` short i32
multiply-accumulate loops over a `win2 x win2` upper-triangular i32 scratch
(`_mm256_mullo_epi32` on widened lanes, 8 products per instruction pair, an
average slice length of 13 with a scalar tail), and flushed the scratch to
i64 once per row: ~1,900 Ir per pixel for `win2 (win2 + 3) / 2` = 350
products at win = 5. C forms 2 W^2 + (W-1)^2 = 66 products per pixel
(`_mm256_madd_epi16`, 16 per instruction) and derives the other 284 `H`
entries from O(width + height) edge deltas — ~15 Ir per pixel. The 127x is
5.3x more products times ~24x more instructions per product.

=================== C's STRUCTURE (cited) ===================

`svt_av1_compute_stats_avx2` (ASM_AVX2/pickrst_avx2.c:2345): find_average,
`sub_avg_block_avx2` (:202) into i16 `d` (window support, stride rounded to
16) and `s` (source), then `compute_stats_win5_avx2` (:775) or
`compute_stats_win7_avx2` (:1546), then `diagonal_copy_stats_avx2` (:685).
Inside the kernel, writing H as a W x W grid of W x W blocks (block =
column-offset pair, entry = row-offset pair):
  Step 1 (:786) every M entry and block (0, j)'s TOP ROW, full madd dots —
    `stats_top_win*` (:247/:271): load src and dgd once per 16-pixel chunk,
    madd each against the W window rows, 2W register accumulators over the
    WHOLE region (8-bit path; the high-bit-depth path drains every
    `h_allowed` rows, :285).
  Step 2 (:827) block (0, j)'s LEFT COLUMN, full dots — `stats_left_win*`
    (:300/:315).
  Step 3 (:967) diagonal blocks' top rows from the previous diagonal
    block's, by a column-shift delta over the height (`step3_win*`,
    `update_5_stats_avx2`).
  Step 4 (:1185) squares' top row + left column from block (i-1, j-1)'s,
    column-shift deltas gathered with `_mm256_insert_epi16` chains.
  Step 5 (:1404) squares' interiors from (l-1, m-1) by a row-shift delta
    over the width — `derive_square_win*` (:418/:458): msub the top rows,
    madd the bottom rows, `hadd_update_4_stats_avx2` (pickrst_avx2.h:281)
    reduces and adds into H.
  Step 6 (:1470) triangles' interiors the same way — `derive_triangle_win*`
    (:536/:562).
`madd_avx2` / `msub_avx2` (pickrst_avx2.h:235/:240) are `_mm256_madd_epi16`
+ add/sub into i32 lanes; `hadd_four_32_to_64_avx2` widens lanes to i64
BEFORE the cross-lane add. The NEON kernel (ASM_NEON/pickrst_neon.c:147 /
:698, entry :1200) is the same six steps on `vmlal_s16` / `vmlal_high_s16`
(pickrst_neon.h:46).

=================== THE PORT'S ROUTE ===================

One `macro_rules! cs_kernel` body (crates/svtav1-dsp/src/restoration.rs)
with C's six steps, instantiated per ISA and per window size (W = 5 / 7 as
a literal, so the accumulator arrays are register-resident), over seven
per-ISA `#[rite]` lane primitives: a 16-lane i16 load, a lane AND, a zero
accumulator, pairwise multiply-add and multiply-subtract into i32 lanes
(`_mm256_madd_epi16` / `vmlal_s16`+`vmlal_high_s16`), an i64 horizontal
reduce, and a lane mask. Two departures from C, both measured:
  * Steps 3-4's column-shift deltas run over TRANSPOSED strips of `d` (the
    2*hw leftmost and the 2*hw columns at `width..`), built once in
    `cs_prepare`, so they are the same masked madd dot as everything else
    instead of C's scalar `_mm256_insert_epi16` gathers.
  * Steps 1-2 drain their i32 accumulators to i64 every
    `rows_per_drain = floor(i32::MAX / (chunks * 130050))` rows (C's 8-bit
    path never drains and relies on the unit-size bound); with the
    `CS_MAX_DIM = 32000` structural guard every accumulator bound is a
    computed number, not a comment.
Row views are exact-length `&[[i16; 16]]` slices built with plain loops —
NOT `core::array::from_fn`, which is not inlined and hid the lengths so
LLVM kept a `cmp; je` per chunk per row (measured: 16.88 M -> 8.37 M Ir when
replaced). The steps 3-4 top-row and left-column accumulations are two
passes so each keeps <= W accumulators in registers (the fused form spilled
at W = 7). `find_average` got AVX2 (`_mm256_sad_epu8`) / NEON
(`vpaddlq_u8` -> `vpadalq_u32`) arms (8.37 M -> 7.93 M).

WHY NOT `#[magetypes]`: the shape needs a pairwise widening i16 x i16 -> i32
multiply-accumulate (`_mm256_madd_epi16` / `vmlal_s16`), which magetypes
has at no version (0.9.28 pinned; `origin/main` has `widen_low/high` but
no `madd`); widen + `mullo_epi32` + add is 3-6x the instructions of one
madd and would have left the kernel at ~5x C. The missing primitive is
`i16x16::madd_adjacent(i16x16) -> i32x8` (and its `msub`); with it the
seven primitives collapse and this body becomes one generic
`#[magetypes]` function.

Iterations, all on photo_cid p6, all byte-identical, all
`c_parity_wiener` 5/5 with `permutations_run >= 2`:
  746.55 M  before (per-pixel gather + win2 + 1 = 26 mac_row calls per pixel at win 5)
   18.49 M  C-shape, `&[i16]` loads with per-load `[..16]` checks
   16.88 M  exact-length chunk slices via `core::array::from_fn` (not inlined)
    8.37 M  chunk slices built inline; steps 3-4 split into two passes
    7.93 M  + SIMD find_average                        <- landed

=================== BYTE-IDENTITY ===================

Every intermediate is an exact integer: products of two values in
[-255, 255] fit i32; each madd lane holds <= 2 * chunks * 65025 products
between drains (steps 1-2) or in total (deltas), bounded by CS_MAX_DIM;
lanes are widened to i64 before any cross-lane add; the shift recurrences
are exact identities. So each M/H entry is the same finite sum of the same
products the scalar reference forms, and for exact integers a sum does not
depend on its association. Pinned by `tests/c_parity_wiener.rs`
(`compute_stats_matches_c`, `compute_stats_all_tiers_match_c` — 220
iterations, widths 1..90, both windows, every tier, asserting
`permutations_run >= 2` and no excluded token) against real C on BOTH
ISAs: aarch64 (this Mac) 5/5, x86_64 (r7900x) 5/5.

